 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Boundary Tetrahedra:** Tetrahedra intersecting block boundaries must be handled logically to ensure consistent ordering. Failure to do so may result in visual artifacts or incorrect compositing [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
-*   **Occlusion Testing:** The `is_unobstructed` function requires accurate geometric tests. Approximations may lead to incorrect sorting [G].
-*   **Precision:** Floating-point precision issues may arise in depth comparisons, especially for large datasets or extreme viewing angles [G].
+*   **Cyclic Dependencies:** If tetrahedra mutually occlude each other in a cycle, the peeling process may deadlock. The pseudocode includes a fallback to break the deadlock [G].
+*   **Boundary Ambiguity:** Tetrahedra near block boundaries must be handled carefully to avoid double-counting or gaps. Logical partitioning is used to resolve this [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
+*   **Precision:** Floating-point precision in occlusion checks may lead to incorrect sorting. Robust geometric predicates are recommended [G].
 
